# Select a row, then overwrite a column

A click stores the row id. A second control holds the new value. A button writes that value into one column of that row. The column can be status, name, or any other column on the input table.

1. On select on the clicked column. Set control value from the system column Row ID (the column titled `ID`) into `v.id_<clicked column>_selected`. A click on `name` writes `v.id_name_selected`.
2. The new value is a control the user changes, so it is `c.<name>`. Name it for the column it writes: `c.status` into `status`, `c.name` into `name`.
3. On the button, On click, effect Update row(s). In the input table. Update row(s) by Single row. The row id comes from `v.id_<clicked column>_selected`. The column comes from the `c.` control.

Run add-column when the column is new, then add the id control, then set-action on-select, then add the value control, then add the button, then set-action update-row. Publish once. Existing rows stay empty until the button writes one.
